WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.275
Lesson 8.4.

00:00:02.275 --> 00:00:06.065
The operating playbook: deploy, monitor, respond, review.

00:00:06.065 --> 00:00:08.301
By the end of this lesson, you'll be able

00:00:08.301 --> 00:00:11.390
to run every position through the same four-phase routine.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:13.980
Here's the plan.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.665
First, the key ideas.

00:00:15.665 --> 00:00:18.380
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:19.905
Then, your checklist.

00:00:19.905 --> 00:00:22.067
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:27.853
First, Deploy: due diligence done · before-signing checklist

00:00:27.853 --> 00:00:31.236
· test amount · journal row (protocol, chain,

00:00:31.236 --> 00:00:35.728
contracts, amount, entry, thesis, kill rules, approvals).

00:00:35.728 --> 00:00:41.523
Next, Monitor: daily HF/pegs/ranges/incidents; weekly P&L vs

00:00:41.523 --> 00:00:46.763
benchmark, harvest, revoke; monthly register review.

00:00:46.763 --> 00:00:50.071
Then, Respond: pre-written actions for each

00:00:50.071 --> 00:00:53.378
trigger (see Module 11.5 for incidents).

00:00:53.378 --> 00:00:56.871
And finally, Review: net return after all costs vs

00:00:56.871 --> 00:01:01.186
benchmark; simplify anything you can't explain in one sentence.

00:01:02.486 --> 00:01:06.991
Position: USDC supply, Protocol Y, Arbitrum.

00:01:06.991 --> 00:01:13.901
Amount / date: $10,000 · 2026-09-01.

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:17.356
Thesis: ~5% from real borrow demand.

00:01:17.356 --> 00:01:20.909
Kill rules: Utilisation > 95% for 48h;

00:01:20.909 --> 00:01:25.036
oracle or collateral change; any incident.

00:01:25.036 --> 00:01:30.696
Approvals: USDC → Protocol Y pool, limited to $10,000.

00:01:30.696 --> 00:01:34.222
Weekly: Interest earned, utilisation, governance notes.

00:01:35.523 --> 00:01:36.983
Here's your checklist.

00:01:36.983 --> 00:01:38.518
Do it now, for real.

00:01:38.518 --> 00:01:41.143
First, Journal row for every position.

00:01:41.143 --> 00:01:42.699
Next, Daily / weekly /

00:01:42.699 --> 00:01:45.163
monthly routine in the calendar.

00:01:45.163 --> 00:01:47.983
And finally, Response actions written per trigger.

00:01:49.283 --> 00:01:50.493
Question 1.

00:01:50.493 --> 00:01:51.583
The four phases?

00:01:56.003 --> 00:01:58.823
The answer: Deploy, monitor, respond, review.

00:02:00.123 --> 00:02:01.368
Question 2.

00:02:01.368 --> 00:02:02.783
What goes in a journal row?

00:02:07.203 --> 00:02:10.062
The answer: Position, amount, date, thesis,

00:02:10.062 --> 00:02:12.792
kill rules, approvals and ongoing results.

00:02:14.092 --> 00:02:15.362
Question 3.

00:02:15.362 --> 00:02:16.330
What to do with a

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:18.157
strategy you can't explain simply?

00:02:22.577 --> 00:02:24.847
The answer: Simplify it or exit.

00:02:26.147 --> 00:02:27.392
Let's recap.

00:02:27.392 --> 00:02:31.697
Deploy: due diligence done · before-signing checklist ·

00:02:31.697 --> 00:02:35.302
test amount · journal row (protocol, chain.

00:02:35.302 --> 00:02:39.857
Monitor: daily HF/pegs/ranges/incidents.

00:02:39.857 --> 00:02:43.301
Respond: pre-written actions for each trigger

00:02:43.301 --> 00:02:45.997
(see Module 11.5 for incidents).

00:02:45.997 --> 00:02:49.322
Review: net return after all costs vs benchmark.

00:02:50.622 --> 00:02:53.137
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:53.137 --> 00:02:57.072
Next up, Lesson 8.5: Measuring performance honestly.
